<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 12+ (API 31) splash screen.

  From API 31 the system ALWAYS draws a splash: with no attributes set it uses the launcher
  icon, which is why removing MAUI's generated theme made the app open on a large rendition of
  its own icon rather than the Nassau Records title.

  The PNGs are MAUI's own conversion of Resources/Splash/splash_nassau.svg, lifted out of the
  last AAB it built and checked in as ordinary drawables - Android cannot consume the SVG
  directly, and re-deriving it by hand would risk a different result than shipped before.

  WHY splash_icon RATHER THAN splash_nassau. The shipped splash_nassau.png is a fully
  OPAQUE BLACK 576x576 square whose white title sits at y 457..518 - wide, and near the
  bottom. The API 31+ splash masks its icon to a circle and only the inner two thirds
  survive, so that title lands outside the mask and the splash renders as pure black. Two
  earlier attempts failed on this: putting the image in the icon slot unchanged (masked away)
  and moving it to windowBackground (that surface only shows until the first rendered frame,
  and SDL creates its GL surface immediately).

  splash_icon.png is generated from splash_nassau.png: the title is cropped to its bounding
  box and centred on a TRANSPARENT square 1.5x its width, so it occupies two thirds of the
  frame and fits the mask whole. Transparent because windowSplashScreenBackground already
  paints black - baking the background in is what made the original unusable here.

  Regenerate with the snippet in the WP-6.1 commit message if the artwork ever changes.
-->
<resources>
  <style name="SiliconDesert.Theme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Material.NoActionBar.Fullscreen">
    <item name="android:windowBackground">@drawable/splash_window</item>
    <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
    <item name="android:windowFullscreen">true</item>

    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenBackground">@android:color/black</item>
    <item name="android:windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@drawable/splash_icon</item>
  </style>
</resources>
